      "claim": "A human can survive without water for at most about 7 days (≈168 hours) under optimal, low‑activity conditions.",
      "evidence": "Medical literature (WHO, US Army Field Manual) cites 3–5 days typical, with the absolute upper limit around 7 days in cool, low‑stress environments.",
